====================================
PROJECT OVERVIEW
====================================
Project Name: Digital Service Request Management System (DSRMS)

Purpose:
An API-first backend system that allows users to register, authenticate,
and create/manage service requests with role-based access, status tracking,
and audit logging.

====================================
TECH STACK
====================================
- Node.js
- Express.js
- PostgreSQL
- JWT authentication
- bcrypt for password hashing
- Jest + Supertest for testing
- dotenv for configuration

====================================
DATABASE LOGIC (MUST FOLLOW)
====================================
Tables:
1. users
   - id (UUID, PK)
   - email (unique)
   - password_hash
   - role (USER, ADMIN)
   - is_active
   - created_at
   - updated_at

2. service_requests
   - id (UUID, PK)
   - title
   - description
   - category
   - priority (LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH)
   - status (OPEN, IN_PROGRESS, RESOLVED)
   - created_by (FK → users.id)
   - assigned_to (FK → users.id, nullable)
   - created_at
   - updated_at

3. request_audits
   - id (UUID, PK)
   - request_id (FK → service_requests.id)
   - changed_by (FK → users.id)
   - old_status
   - new_status
   - note
   - changed_at

Business rules:
- Only ADMIN can change request status
- Status flow: OPEN → IN_PROGRESS → RESOLVED
- Users can only modify their own requests
- All status changes must be logged in request_audits

